# crtulum script — a scripted run with a Microsoft Agent character commentating.
#
#   crtulum --fetch-agent Merlin           # once: pull the sprite sheet down
#   crtulum --render out.mp4 --script examples/agent.crts
#
# The character is composited into the *signal*, before the tube — so he's made of
# phosphor like everything else on the screen. Scanlines run across him, the mask
# breaks him into RGB stripes, and when he moves he trails red as the green and blue
# phosphors decay out from under him.

# ---- setup ----------------------------------------------------------------
rom      "game.nes"            # quote anything with spaces in it
frames   1200
size     1280x960
ssaa     2
preset   trinitron
camera   yaw=0.0 pitch=0.06 dist=2.6

agent    merlin                # or clippy, genie, peedy, rover, links, …

# ---- the run --------------------------------------------------------------
# Inputs land on exact frames; the character runs on the wall clock beside them.

at 1.0      press start
frame 240   hold right
frame 512   press a for 18 frames
frame 700   release right

# ---- the commentary -------------------------------------------------------
# Coordinates are normalised to the picture: 0,0 is the top-left of the raster and
# 1,1 the bottom-right, so they don't change when the signal resolution does.

at 0.2   agent at 0.78,0.66            # park him bottom-right, where Clippy always sat
at 0.5   agent show                    # plays the character's own entrance
at 1.5   agent say "This run saves four frames on the first jump."

at 6.0   agent point 0.30,0.62         # turn and gesture at part of the picture
at 6.4   agent say "Right here."

at 9.0   agent move to 0.22,0.30 over 1.2   # walks, playing his Move animation
at 11.0  agent play Congratulate       # any animation the character has, by name
at 13.0  agent hide

# Between instructions he falls back to his rest pose, and after a few idle seconds
# he'll start one of his own idle animations — the same behaviour he had on the
# desktop. `crtulum --agent merlin` with no script gets you exactly that.
